WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.467
-Our next guest has
her comedy album, "Perm Day,"

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:06.501
available at MaryMackComedy.com.

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:08.968
Please welcome the very funny
Mary Mack.

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:11.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:12.968
-Hi, Jimmy!

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.701
Hey, guys!

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:18.234
Thank you!
Oh, man.

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:20.234
Thanks!
Thank you so much!

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:22.367
I -- I am Mary Mack.

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:23.667
[ Laughter ]
Oh.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:27.200
Guys, I was so excited
to be here, I put on makeup.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.200
I know. They say you
gotta blend it in.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.667
I'm not blending it in.

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:34.934
I want to get somewhere and have
people be like, "She tried."

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:39.133
Right?
It's hard to age as a woman.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:41.701
I got -- I got a mole
on my face now,

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:43.434
keeps sprouting out a hair.

00:00:43.434 --> 00:00:45.634
I cut it, it sprouts,
I cut it, it sprouts.

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:48.267
I can't keep up.
It's like mowing the yard.

00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:49.534
All right?
Yeah.

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:52.400
I'm thinking about getting
a neighbor kid to cut it.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:59.167
I grew up in Northern Wisconsin.

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:00.934
Yeah.
Not fancy, yeah.

00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:04.067
We -- We didn't -- We didn't get
a spring break in school.

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:07.200
Instead, we got a week off
in November for deer hunting.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.734
Yeah, 'cause with a freezer
full of venison,

00:01:11.734 --> 00:01:13.901
who cares if you graduate?

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:17.167
Yeah.

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:20.501
[ Chuckles ]
Yeah.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:23.400
One time in school,
the teacher's decided to have

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.300
a "healthy lifestyles day."

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.701
It's never been attempted
before or since

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.133
in the state of Wisconsin.

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:31.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:33.133
But I took a class.
It was called

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:35.000
"How to slow your breathing down

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.234
in case you fall through
the ice."

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:40.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:45.033
But it wasn't even taught by,
like, a expert or a park ranger.

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:48.033
It was just some guy
who fell through the ice...

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:50.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.901 --> 00:01:52.667
...and figured it out.

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:55.133
My mom is retired up there
in the woods,

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:57.334
and she has no Internet
or cable news,

00:01:57.334 --> 00:02:00.834
so she has to have
her own thoughts.

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:02.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:04.868
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:10.667
My mom is pro-trans rights,
and she enjoys burning plastic.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:13.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.501
Yeah.
You can't pigeon-hole Jan.

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:19.000
You can't.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.534
My mom is from that very bland
Scandinavian country

00:02:21.534 --> 00:02:24.400
called Duluth, Minnesota.
You ever --

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.200
Oh, good.
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.734
She's never even
had yogurt before.

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:30.334
Mnh-mnh.
Too spicy.

00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:34.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:37.167
She's working with
an old Swedish taste palate.

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:39.634
"Oh, chives on a baked potato?

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:41.400
What, are they trying
to kill me?"

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:45.667
Guys, there's a lot of heat in
a -- it can sneak up on you.

00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:46.934
Okay? Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.934 --> 00:02:50.000
Chives are like the habanero
of Minnesota, all right?

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.467
Yeah.

00:02:54.467 --> 00:02:57.934
Anyway, my whole family, they're
so much tougher than I am.

00:02:57.934 --> 00:02:59.734
I got one brother, Scott.

00:02:59.734 --> 00:03:02.734
He got ran over by the bulldozer
a few years ago.

00:03:02.734 --> 00:03:04.467
[ Audience "Oohs" ]
No, he's fine.

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:05.534
He's fine.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.534 --> 00:03:07.334
He's almost more normal now.

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:09.601
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:10.834
But think about that.

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:12.734
The bulldozer,
that doesn't have wheels.

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:14.701
That has tracks.
Tracks!

00:03:14.701 --> 00:03:18.767
So it takes a long time
to get ran over by it.

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:19.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:20.968
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:22.701
You got to be patient.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.901
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:26.334
Not me.
I'm not tough.

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:28.501
I -- the toughest thing
I ever did was,

00:03:28.501 --> 00:03:31.434
I ate organic food last week.

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:32.634
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, the whole week.

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:35.467
Oh, man.
I had organic maple bacon fudge.

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:37.534
Do you ever --
you ever have organic maple --

00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:39.367
it's hard to get it organic.

00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:41.234
Pbht!
There's a lot of layers.

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:42.701
[ Laughter ]
Yeah? Yeah.

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:47.000
The fudge, that's got to be,
like, cage-free or something.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:51.434
Most people like
to pre-package their fudge.

00:03:51.434 --> 00:03:55.400
That is not a euphemism.
That is a USDA regulation.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.767 --> 00:04:01.767
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:03.400
And then you got the bacon.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.501
That --
oh, think about the pig.

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:08.701
The pig has to be like,
"Oh, okay, fine."

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:10.300
The pig has to give consent.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.400
Otherwise, it's not organic.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:13.567
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:16.300
Yeah, that pig
has a safe word, too.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.634
If he oinks twice
before the conveyor belt,

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:21.501
he gets to go to a community
college of his choice.

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:24.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:25.467
All right.

00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:27.133
Little too weird.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:29.667
All right.

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:31.300
All right.
Before I go, I just want

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:34.467
to let you know about a service
I'm offering.

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:37.467
You can see me -- if you're
having problems sleeping,

00:04:37.467 --> 00:04:39.767
come see me after the show.

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:41.834
What I do,
I rent my husband out to you.

00:04:41.834 --> 00:04:44.200
He comes over,
stands next to your bed,

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.400
and tells you about

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.033
his fantasy-football team
for a while.

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:50.300
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:53.367
Five minutes, and you're out.
I'm almost med-free!

00:04:53.367 --> 00:04:55.400
Yeah!
Thank you so much!

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.667
I'm Mary Mack!
Happy holidays!

00:04:57.667 --> 00:05:00.534
-Almost med-free?
Almost?

00:05:00.534 --> 00:05:02.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:05.367
Mary Mack, everybody!

00:05:05.367 --> 00:05:08.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's exactly right.

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:11.601
Check out "Perm Day"
at MaryMackComedy.com.

00:05:11.601 --> 00:05:13.968
We'll be right back,
ladies and gentlemen.

